  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[guns-for-ducks]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[Guns for Ducks]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[The bread stops here. Water pistols for the worthy.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Quack Holster
Bread Radar
Splash Mode
Pond Permit]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Arm every pond in the country | Water pistols for all ducks. Rollout starts in the capital, like everything else.
End the stale bread era | Strategic initiative: no more week-old white loaf. The ducks demand sourdough or nothing.
Pond-as-a-Service | Every pond gets an API. Nobody knows what it returns. Probably 'quack'.
Tiny holster supply chain | Size XXS, waterproof, wing-accessible. Procurement is confused but trying.
Go-to-pond strategy | Win the mallard market first, then swans. The swans have not replied to our emails.
Compliance with pond law | Legal must define 'duck'. Legal has requested three workshops and a site visit.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Squirt back | As a duck, I want to squirt back so that people think twice before throwing toast at my head.
Quick-draw holster | As a mallard, I want a holster that fits wet feathers so that I can quick-draw mid-paddle.
Refill from pond | As a duck, I want to reload straight from the pond so that I never run out. I live in the ammo.
Hunter early warning | As a duck, I want a push notification when someone in green shows up so that I can act casual.
Duckling safety lock | As a mother duck, I want a child lock so that the ducklings stop soaking each other at dinner.
Quack-activated trigger | As a duck with no fingers, I want voice control so that one quack means go and two mean stop.
Bread quality rating | As a duck, I want to rate bread 1 to 5 so that the man with the rye crusts takes the hint.
Ducks in a row | As a project manager, I want the ducks in a row so that I can finally say it and mean it.
Swan diplomacy | As a duck, I want a peace treaty with the swans so that we only fight on one front.
Goose escalation path | As a duck, I want to escalate to a goose so that serious cases are handled by a professional.
Jogger exemption | As a jogger, I want to be whitelisted so that I stop arriving at work mysteriously damp.
Indoor demo | As a client, I want the demo indoors so that my laptop survives. Request denied by the ducks.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Splash Mode | Wide spray for groups. Recommended for school trips with sandwich bags.
Bread Radar | Detects incoming bread within 30 metres. Beeps twice for croissant.
Tiny safety goggles | Ordered in duck size. Delivered in adult human. Ticket raised.
Pond Permit | A laminated licence with photo ID. All the photos are the same duck.
Waterproof manual | Onboarding in pictograms. Step 1: quack. Step 2: aim. Step 3: quack.
Camouflage skin | Makes the water pistol look like a reed. Makes the duck look suspicious.
Rain mode | Does nothing at all. The ducks are delighted anyway.
Formation mode | Synchronised spray across a V-formation. Requires one duck who can count.
Low water alert | Warns you when the tank is empty. Suggested fix: look down.
Quack translation | Translates 'quack' into 12 languages. All 12 are 'quack'.
Friendly fire filter | Stops ducks soaking other ducks. Switched off by the ducks within a day.
Holster cup holder | Because the persona workshop said ducks 'value convenience'.
Winter mode | On frozen ponds it throws very small snowballs. Battery life: four minutes.
Webbed-foot login | Biometric sign-in by footprint. Fails if the duck has been standing in mud. So: always.
Ceasefire button | Pauses everything when someone brings oats instead of bread.
Honk add-on | Optional goose sound for intimidation. Licensed per honk.]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Duck squirts itself | Repro: duck looks into the nozzle. Happens every time. Ducks refuse to read the docs.
Holster only fits left wing | Right-winged ducks are blocked. Workaround: swim in circles.
Radar flags the bakery as hostile | The whole bakery on the corner shows as incoming bread. The ducks are mobilising.
Water pistol leaks in water | Cannot tell if it is leaking. It is in a pond. Closed as 'cannot reproduce'.
Geese got admin access | Nobody knows how. They changed the logo to a goose and locked us out.
Rubber duck issued a permit | A bath duck is licensed and top of the leaderboard. It has not moved once.
Quack trigger fires in meetings | A developer said 'quack' at standup. Three colleagues soaked. Works as designed?
Decoys in the user table | 40% of accounts are made of wood. Marketing calls it 'strong organic growth'.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[pond_final_FINAL.sql | The only database backup. It is on a USB stick shaped like a duck.
Aim logic from Stack Overflow | The answer had minus three votes. It is now the core of the product.
Hardcoded pond | The whole system assumes one pond in Odense. 'We will scale later,' someone said in 2021.
Duck.cs is 9,000 lines | One class: Duck. It also handles payments, email and Easter.
A cron job named Donald | Runs every night at 03:00. Nobody knows what it does. Nobody dares to stop Donald.
Feathers in the server | Physical tech debt. Ops stopped asking. The fan now makes a soft quacking sound.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[CEO Request: Can the ducks have drones? | 'Just a thought.' The thought was sent to the whole company at 23:14.
CEO Request: Make it B2B | 'Ducks have no budget. Who is the buyer?' Fair. Painful, but fair.
CEO Request: A duck at the julefrokost | 'For the keynote. A real one. With the tiny holster.' Facility has not been told.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[No more stale bread. The pond is armed.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[Tiny holsters, water pistols and a firm quack for ducks who have had enough of dry white bread. Nobody gets hurt. Somebody gets damp.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Get your tiny holster]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Water-based deterrence | Every water pistol is filled straight from the pond. Sustainable, refillable and legal in every park we asked.
Tiny holsters, big energy | Hand-stitched for wing access in under 0.4 seconds. Fits mallards, teals and one very confident swan.
Bread threat detection | Our AI tells rye from white toast at 30 metres. Rye may pass. Toast gets a warning squirt.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[I threw one slice of white toast and was soaked in four seconds. Fair.
Quack. Quack quack. QUACK. (Translation: finally, a vendor that listens.)
The holster fits. The pistol leaks. Apparently the fix is in Q3.
My kids now bring oats and a written apology. The pond has never been calmer.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[Free for ducks. Geese pay double, and they know why. Swans: enterprise, call for a quote.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© Guns for Ducks. Water only. No ducks, humans or baguettes were harmed. The swans have their own terms.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
